# Executing Flows

## Overview

`Jido.Exec` compiles Actions and Flows to native Runic workflows. Runic owns
scheduling and durable runtime state.

Run the cells from top to bottom.

## Install The Package

```elixir
Mix.install([{:jido_action, "~> 3.0.0-beta.12"}])
```

## Define Actions And A Flow

```elixir
defmodule FlowExecution.Add do
  use Jido.Action, name: "flow_execution_add"

  @impl true
  def run(%{left: left, right: right}, _context) do
    {:ok, %{value: left + right}}
  end
end

defmodule FlowExecution.Combine do
  use Jido.Action, name: "flow_execution_combine"

  @impl true
  def run(%{left: left, right: right}, _context) do
    {:ok, %{total: left + right}}
  end
end

defmodule FlowExecution.Diamond do
  use Jido.Flow, name: "flow_execution_diamond"

  flow do
    step "left",
      action: FlowExecution.Add,
      params: %{left: input(:value), right: 1}

    step "right",
      action: FlowExecution.Add,
      params: %{left: input(:value), right: 2}

    step "combine",
      action: FlowExecution.Combine,
      params: %{
        left: result("left", :value),
        right: result("right", :value)
      }

    output(%{result: result("combine")})
  end
end
```

## Run To Completion

```elixir
{:ok, %{result: %{total: 13}}} =
  Jido.Exec.run(FlowExecution.Diamond, %{value: 5})
```

Independent ready work can run concurrently:

```elixir
{:ok, result} =
  Jido.Exec.run(
    FlowExecution.Diamond,
    %{value: 5},
    %{},
    max_concurrency: 2
  )
```

## Compile And Inspect

```elixir
{:ok, %Runic.Workflow{} = workflow} =
  Jido.Exec.compile(FlowExecution.Diamond)

Runic.Workflow.build_log(workflow)
```

The result is the executable graph. It contains real Runic components and
edges. Jido does not create a separate execution-plan struct.

## Observe Failure

```elixir
defmodule FlowExecution.Fail do
  use Jido.Action, name: "flow_execution_fail"

  @impl true
  def run(_params, _context), do: {:error, :not_available}
end

defmodule FlowExecution.Failing do
  use Jido.Flow, name: "flow_execution_failing"

  flow do
    step "fail", action: FlowExecution.Fail, params: %{}
    output(%{result: result("fail")})
  end
end
```

```elixir
{:error, error} = Jido.Exec.run(FlowExecution.Failing)
Exception.message(error)
```

The Action error fails its Runic Runnable. With the default policy, a terminal
failure stops later dispatch.

## Managed Execution

A supervised application can start the same compiled Flow under a
`Runic.Runner`:

```elixir
{:ok, runner} = Runic.Runner.start_link(name: FlowExecution.Runner)

{:ok, _worker} =
  Jido.Exec.start(
    FlowExecution.Runner,
    "diamond-1",
    FlowExecution.Diamond,
    %{value: 5},
    %{},
    checkpoint_strategy: :every_cycle
  )
```

```elixir
{:ok, workflow} = Runic.Runner.get_workflow(FlowExecution.Runner, "diamond-1")
Jido.Exec.result(workflow)
```

Use `Runic.Runner.checkpoint/2` and `stop/3` for durable lifecycle control.
Resume with `Jido.Exec.resume/4` and the same context and options. The Runic Store contains progress. Flow JSON contains only the
portable definition.
